    'transfer.speed.max': 'Maximum: and more Longhorn threads',
    'transfer.speed.tip': 'Economical copies one disk at a time: gentle on a busy cluster. Normal copies every disk at once: Longhorn compresses each on one core, so several go faster, at the cost of CPU on the source and of network. Maximum also raises Longhorn\'s backup and restore threads from 2 to 8 for the transfer: more CPU and network on every node of both clusters, shared with any other backup running meanwhile; put back at the end, even on failure.',
